<p>Hi there, thanks for the reply and critique! Let me start off with clearing up a couple of minor points. First, I did originally try to draft this using the typical SCP-XXXX placeholder but it was ruining my focus on the draft as I couldn't make it flow properly with those X's bothering me, so I went with a provisional number instead. Its purely a measure to ease my writing conscience. And a lot of the SCPs here seem to use 5x5x5 in their containment design anyway, didn't want to buck the trend. Also helped for calculating some math in regards to the amount of time it takes for this skip to alter the air in a room or add anomalous gas to the atmosphere, since 5 is a prime number and all.</p>
<p>As for the revised containment protocols, yeah you're probably right that they should be at the top but I was hesitant, I have seen articles have revised containment procedures listed at the bottom sometimes accompanied by the words 'pending approval' and that was the thing I was aiming for with that. Also I was worried that the revision may give something away in regards to the story, for now they stay where they are but I'm 50/50 about moving them.</p>
<p>Now for the meat amongst the potatoes! You hit one of my biggest concerns/weaknesses on the head, I do struggle with show vs. tell a lot. It's not an easy thing for me to overcome and its not from lack of trying. Your critique here was super helpful with that, and the lines you have pointed out as superfluous or lacklustre have been altered with your feedback. I'm hoping it's an improvement over the original!</p>

