<li>Primarily my problem with this draft is the complete lack of a narrative. This is a series of test logs and observations concerning the anomaly in overly detailed manner. What its missing is an exploration of themes or a narrative arc. Ask yourself:
<ul>
<li>what you want the reader to come away with from this story and</li>
<li>if it might be better with someone to relate to…</li>
<li>also why is this anomaly interesting to you? Other than it being a fan that changes the molecular makeup of the atmosphere around it… what is it you want to say?</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p><em>As it stands right now, this is very dry.</em></p>
<ul>
<li>in terms of small edits, I think you should do away with the testing logs. I think you could summarize the logs in a paragraph in a sub-section labelled “Testing Results” and it would be more efficient. Right now they’re bloat to be cut in my opinion.</li>
</ul>

